== CURRENT STEP: Phase 0b step 2 - interfaces, registries, LayerSpec, generic block (D15) ==
Done when: tests/test_model_contracts.py passes, and tests/test_phase0b_golden.py plus the
existing suite stay green.

[ ] core/registry.py
      Registry(kind): register(name) decorator (duplicate -> ValueError),
      get(name) (unknown -> KeyError listing available names), names().
      Instances: MIXERS, FFNS, RESIDUALS, TOKEN_MEMORIES, OUTPUT_HEADS.

[ ] core/interfaces.py
      runtime_checkable Protocols:
        SequenceMixer  forward(x [T,D], meta, state) -> (update [T,D], AuxOutputs); .capabilities
        FeedForward    forward(x [T,D], meta) -> (update [T,D], AuxOutputs); post_step()
        TokenMemory    forward(x [T,D], meta) -> (update [T,D], AuxOutputs)   (no impl yet)
        Residual       init(x0) / read(state, i) / write(state, i, update) / final(state)
        OutputHead     forward(h [T,D], meta) -> (logits [T,V], AuxOutputs)
      MixerCaps: frozen dataclass; chunked_prefill, prefix_snapshot, rollback,
      context_parallel, needs_positions (all default False).

[ ] model_config.py
      LayerSpec(mixer="gqa", ffn="moe", memory=None).
      ModelConfig.layers defaults to num_layers copies; wrong length -> ValueError.
      ModelConfig.residual = "standard", ModelConfig.output_head = "lm".

[ ] Attention -> MIXERS "gqa"
      constructor (config, layer_idx); forward(x, meta, state) -> (update, AuxOutputs());
      capabilities = MixerCaps(needs_positions=True) and nothing else.

[ ] MoE -> FFNS "moe"
      constructor (config, layer_idx); forward(x, meta) -> (update, aux).
      Router bias update leaves forward: accumulate routing stats during training
      forwards only; apply them in post_step(); a second post_step with nothing new,
      or after eval forwards, changes nothing.

[ ] model/residual.py -> RESIDUALS "standard"
      init -> x0; read -> state; write -> state + update (new tensor, never in place);
      final -> state. Sublayer index i = 2 * layer_idx + (0 mixer, 1 ffn).

[ ] LM head -> OUTPUT_HEADS "lm"
      constructor (config, embedding); owns the final norm and the projection,
      whose weight is the embedding weight (tied).

[ ] model/components.py
      imports every implementation module so the registries are populated.

[ ] DecoderBlock
      built from its LayerSpec through the registries; attributes mixer, mixer_norm,
      ffn, ffn_norm. forward takes and returns the residual state:
      read -> norm -> mixer -> write -> read -> norm -> ffn -> write; aux merged
      under "mixer" and "ffn".

[ ] TransformerLM
      residual and head from registries; forward(meta, states=None);
      post_step() calls post_step() on every FFN.

[ ] Trainer
      call model.post_step() once after the optimizer steps in train_step.

[ ] model/checkpoint_migration.py
      migrate_state_dict: blocks.{i}.attention/attn_norm/moe/moe_norm ->
      mixer/mixer_norm/ffn/ffn_norm; final_norm -> head.norm; lm_head -> head.proj;
      no-op on new-format keys.
      Apply in inference/generation_setup.py AND training/checkpoint.py.

[ ] Checks while refactoring
      - Muon picks parameters by leaf name (q_proj.weight, up_weight, ...) in
        training/optim/build.py: keep those names or update use_muon.
      - Optimizer state in training checkpoints is stored by parameter position:
        resuming an old training checkpoint only works if parameter order is
        unchanged. Keep the order, or resume old checkpoints with fresh optimizer state.

[ ] Tell Claude when pushed: outdated tests that build Attention/MoE directly or use
    old attribute names get updated then.

[ ] Run on the GPU machine: tests/test_core_contracts.py (step 1, still unrun),
    tests/test_model_contracts.py, tests/test_phase0b_golden.py, full suite.
  Checks to watch for:
  - LM head ties by sharing the Parameter, not by storing the embedding module
    (a stored module adds a head.embedding.weight key that old checkpoints lack).
  - Keep parameter registration order (norm, mixer, norm, ffn; head.norm then head.proj),
    so saved optimizer state still lines up with parameters on resume.
  - Routing statistics: accumulate expert counts (not fractions) in training forwards only;
    the accumulators are non-persistent buffers, reset in post_step.
  - ModelConfig with LayerSpec must still save to JSON (checkpoint.py dumps __dict__).
  - migrate_state_dict also needed when resuming training (training/checkpoint.py), not just generate_setup.


